    "result": "I fixed `Broken` in `links.go`, but I could not run the tests because the `go test` command needs your approval.\n\nThe cause was a data race: all goroutines appended to one shared `broken` slice at the same time, so some appends were lost. Now each goroutine records a pass or fail for its own part of the list only, with the same chunks and the same number of goroutines. After they finish, one loop collects the failing links in input order.\n\nI also changed two other things:\n- A `workers` value below 1 is now treated as 1. Before, 0 caused a divide-by-zero panic.\n- I added `links_test.go`, which checks the result against the expected list for several worker counts.\n\nTo verify, run `go test -race ./...`.",
